93present%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"1000\" data-file-height=\"1000\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" class=\"mw-file-element\">\n     </span>\n    </span>\n   </span>\n   <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatican_City\" title=\"Vatican City\" about=\"#mwt2182\" id=\"mwEas\">\n    Vatican City\n   </a>\n  </td>\n  <td id=\"mwEaw\">\n   <span about=\"#mwt2183\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwEa0\" data-mw=\"{&#34;parts&#34;:[{&#34;template&#34;:{&#34;target&#34;:{&#34;wt&#34;:&#34;km2 mi2&#34;,&#34;href&#34;:&#34;./Template:Km2_mi2&#34;},&#34;params&#34;:{&#34;1&#34;:{&#34;wt&#34;:&#34;0.44&#34;},&#34;2&#34;:{&#34;wt&#34;:&#34;2&#34;},&#34;3&#34;:{&#34;wt&#34;:&#34;d&#34;}},&#34;i&#34;:0}}]}\">\n    0.44 (0.17)\n   </span>\n  </td>\n  <td id=\"mwEa4\">\n   <span about=\"#mwt2184\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwEa8\" data-mw=\"{&#34;parts&#34;:[{&#34;template&#34;:{&#34;target&#34;:{&#34;wt&#34;:&#34;km2 mi2&#34;,&#34;href&#34;:&#34;./Template:Km2_mi2&#34;},&#34;params&#34;:{&#34;1&#34;:{&#34;wt&#34;:&#34;0.44&#34;},&#34;2&#34;:{&#34;wt&#34;:&#34;2&#34;},&#34;3&#34;:{&#34;wt&#34;:&#34;d&#34;}},&#34;i&#34;:0}}]}\">\n    0.44 (0.17)\n   </span>\n  </td>\n  <td id=\"mwEbA\">\n   0\n  </td>\n  <td id=\"mwEbE\">\n   0\n  </td>\n  <td id=\"mwEbI\">\n   <sup about=\"#mwt2185\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-176\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\"{&#34;name&#34;:&#34;ref&#34;,&#34;attrs&#34;:{&#34;group&#34;:&#34;lower-alpha&#34;},&#34;body&#34;:{&#34;id&#34;:&#34;mw-reference-text-cite_note-176&#34;},&#34;parts&#34;:[{&#34;template&#34;:{&#34;target&#34;:{&#34;wt&#34;:&#34;efn&#34;,&#34;href&#34;:&#34;./Template:Efn&#34;},&#34;params&#34;:{&#34;1&#34;:{&#34;wt&#34;:&#34;[[European microstates|European microstate]]. Smallest country in the world. The [[:it:Calendario Atlante De Agostini|De Agostini Atlas Calendar]] listed the area of Vatican City as 0.44 {{km2}} in its 1930 edition&lt;ref&gt;[https://books.google.com/books?id=JqlIZ70Jn9gC&amp;q=vaticano De Agostini Atlas Calendar] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221016055707/https://books.google.com/books?id=JqlIZ70Jn9gC&amp;q=vaticano |date=16 October 2022 }}, 1930, p. 99. {{in lang|it}}&lt;/ref&gt; but corrected it to 0.49 {{km2}} in its 1945–46 edition.&lt;ref name=agostini1945&gt;[https://books.google.com/books?id=ZpJXsBX_6uUC&amp;q=vaticano De Agostini Atlas Calendar] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221016055707/https://books.google.com/books?id=ZpJXsBX_6uUC&amp;q=vaticano |date=16 October 2022 }}, 1945–46, p. 128. {{in lang|it}}&lt;/ref&gt; However, the figure of 0.44&amp;nbsp;{{km2}} is widely cited by many sources (e.g. Encyclopedia Britannica) and it is the official{{Clarify|date=July 2026}} figure.{{Dubious|date=July 2026}}&#34;}},&#34;i&#34;:0}}]}\">\n    <a href=\"#cite_note-176\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwEbM\">\n     <span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwEbQ\">\n      <span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwEbU\">\n       [\n      </span>\n      dk\n      <span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwEbY\">\n       ]\n      </span>\n     </span>\n    </a>\n   </sup>\n  </td>\n </tr>\n</tbody>\n"
